!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = CD8 T cells were FACS-sorted into FCS containing tubes and after sort 10% DMSO were added, mixed and stored at -80°C until all samples were collected. Profiling of Chromatin was performed by ATAC-seq. Cells were thawed and washed in cold PBS and lysed.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = After cell lysis, transposition happened at 42ºC for 45 min. After purification of the DNA with the MinElute PCR purification kit (Qiagen), material was amplified for 5 cycles. Additional PCR cycles were evaluated by real time PCR. Final product was cleaned by Ampure Beads at a 1.5x ratio. Libraries were sequenced on a Hiseq 2500 1T in a 50bp/50bp Paired end run, using the TruSeq SBS Kit v3 (Illumina).  An average of 47x106 paired reads were generated per sample.
!Sample_description = mouse splenocytes
!Sample_data_processing = Library strategy: ATAC-Seq
!Sample_data_processing = Base trimming and quality filtering using TrimGalore! v0.4.0, powered by CutAdapt v1.8.1 and FastQC v0.11.3 using paired and fastqc options
!Sample_data_processing = Alignment using Bowtie2 v2.2.5 using default parameter settings
!Sample_data_processing = conversion to bam, uniq, sort bam using SAMtools v0.1.18
!Sample_data_processing = peak calling using macs2 callpeak v2.1.0.20140616 on merged replicates per sample type, using p-value cutoff of 1e-2, no model, keep-dup=all, call-summits
!Sample_data_processing = IDR per sample to find reproducible peaks, create atlas of reproducible ATAC-seq peaks for both mouse and human
!Sample_data_processing = Counting of reads aligning to atlas peak regions using the summarizeOverlaps function of the R package GenomicAlignments v1.2.2 and GenomicRanges v1.18.4
!Sample_data_processing = Library-size normalized read counts per atlas peak were calculated using DESeq2 v1.6.3
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: mm10 for mus musculus data and hg38 for human samples
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: tab-delimited text file - columns: chromosome, peak start, peak end, gene symbol, gene refseq ID, peak type, DESeq2 size-factor normalized read count for peak
